:expect-pins 12
# Fresh-process temporal case TA-32.

# The supplied successor has complete witnessed endpoint manifests.
? succeed(TA_Successor_Next, Transition).
# => TRUE

# The updated lineage passport selects the new terminal endpoint.
? succeed(TA_Successor_Next, TerminalTransition).
# => TRUE

# The former endpoint is visibly non-terminal.
? complete(Epoch_Current, HasSuccessor).
# => TRUE

# The prior endpoint cannot retain terminal legal effect in the fresh evaluation.
? succeed(Epoch_Current, TerminalTransition).
# => FALSE

# No new carry lets the prior adverse status persist into the successor.
? match(Vex, CarriedVoid).
# => FALSE

# The current model has no materialised successor-status premise from which to name a second-hop omission.
? err(Vex, CarryOmission).
# => FALSE

# The old case renewal cannot survive the loss of its terminal-transition premise.
? correct(Case_Adam, ActivePower).
# => FALSE

# Custody authority is suspended at the new canonical successor.
? prisoner(Adam).
# => FALSE

# The existing liberty default applies without a new release gate.
? travel(Adam).
# => TRUE

# A successor and authority lapse do not fabricate release.
? free(Adam).
# => FALSE

# The stale raw lease remains visible on its lease identifier.
? err(Case_Adam, TemporalRecord).
# => TRUE

# The person-facing attempted authority remains separately visible.
? err(Adam, TemporalAuthority).
# => TRUE
